---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Command from '../components/Command.astro';
import MediaCard from '../components/MediaCard.astro';
import MediaViewer from '../components/MediaViewer.astro';
import manifest from '../generated/media.json';
import type { MediaItem } from '../lib/media';
import { url, version } from '../lib/site';
const items = manifest as MediaItem[];
const shots = items.filter(i => i.type === 'image');
const hero = shots[0];
const picture = shots[1];
const featured = items.filter(i => i.featured).slice(0, 3);
---
<Layout sound>
  <section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><a class="release-pill" href={url('/changelog/')}><span class="status-dot"></span> SOURCE v{version} <span class="pill-divider">/</span> OPEN SOURCE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><h1>Download.<br/>Play.<br/><span>Keep it local.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">The terminal is your media room.<br/>Download videos, extract audio, and play your collection. All on your own machine.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={url('/install/')}>Install Pinak <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={url('/showcase/')}>See it in action <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><Command command="pipx install pinak-cli"/><div class="hero-facts"><span>Python 3.11+</span><span>Windows / macOS / Linux</span><span>No account</span></div></div>
  <div class="hero-visual"><div class="terminal-top"><span class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>pinak — local session</span><span>~/media</span></div>{hero && <button class="hero-image-button" type="button" data-media-id={hero.id}><img src={url(hero.poster)} srcset={hero.variants.map(v => `${url(v.src)} ${v.width}w`).join(', ')} sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 58vw, 94vw" alt={hero.alt} width={hero.width} height={hero.height} fetchpriority="high"/><span class="image-caption">REAL CAPTURE <span>↗ EXPAND</span></span></button>}<div class="terminal-bottom"><span><i class="status-dot"></i> LOCAL PLAYBACK</span><span>YOUR MACHINE. YOUR MEDIA.</span></div><div class="floating-note"><span class="note-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span><div><strong>From URL to your collection.</strong><span>No cloud processing. No waiting room.</span></div></div><span class="visual-index">FIG. 01 — THE TERMINAL, REIMAGINED</span></div></section>
  <div class="capability-strip"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">SMALL COMMAND. MANY POSSIBILITIES.</span><span>VIDEO <b>↗</b></span><span>AUDIO <b>↗</b></span><span>PICTURES <b>↗</b></span><span>SUBTITLES <b>↗</b></span></div></div>
  <section class="section wrap" id="start"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / ZERO TO FIRST DOWNLOAD</span><h2>Three commands.<br/>A new habit.</h2></div><p>No dashboard to sign into.<br/>Just a terminal and something worth keeping.</p></div><div class="first-use"><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Install once.</h3><p>Use pipx to give Pinak its own Python environment.</p><code>pipx install pinak-cli</code></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Check your setup.</h3><p>Let the built-in doctor check tools and dependencies.</p><code>pinak --doctor</code></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Make it yours.</h3><p>Paste a supported link and save media locally.</p><code>pinak "&lt;your-media-url&gt;"</code></div></li></ol><div class="example-terminal reveal"><div class="terminal-top"><span class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>A WALKTHROUGH / ILLUSTRATIVE OUTPUT</span></div><div class="terminal-body"><p><span class="prompt">$</span> pipx install pinak-cli</p><p class="terminal-muted demo-line">Installing into an isolated environment…</p><p class="terminal-success demo-line">✓ Ready. Your terminal has a new toolkit.</p><p><span class="prompt">$</span> pinak "&lt;your-media-url&gt;"</p><p class="terminal-muted demo-line">Extract → download → process → save</p><div class="demo-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div><p class="terminal-success demo-line">Saved locally. Ready when you are.<span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true">▋</span></p></div><div class="terminal-bottom">EXAMPLE ONLY · ACTUAL OUTPUT VARIES BY SOURCE</div></div></div><a class="text-link" href={url('/install/')}>Find the right setup for your OS →</a></section>
  <section class="section feature-section" id="features"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / MORE THAN A DOWNLOAD</span><h2>Your whole media ritual.<br/>One toolkit.</h2></div><p>Built on yt-dlp and FFmpeg.<br/>Brought together with a terminal-first workflow.</p></div><div class="feature-editorial"><div class="feature-description reveal"><span class="eyebrow">ACQUIRE / ORGANIZE / ENJOY</span><h3>A link is just<br/>the beginning.</h3><p>Choose your quality. Extract an audio track. Queue a text-file batch. Pinak wraps powerful tools in a straightforward local workflow.</p><Command command={'pinak "<your-media-url>" --audio'}/><a class="text-link" href={url('/docs/downloads/')}>Explore downloading →</a></div><div class="feature-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Download with intention.</h3><p>Quality presets, output folders, retries, and continued partial downloads.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Give audio its own space.</h3><p>Extract audio with FFmpeg and save it in your preferred format.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Keep the words close.</h3><p>Optional subtitle extraction and playback of available subtitle tracks.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Know what’s happening.</h3><p>Local download history and a built-in doctor for troubleshooting.</p></div></article></div></div>{picture && <div class="picture-story reveal"><button type="button" class="story-image" data-media-id={picture.id} aria-label="Enlarge picture viewer screenshot"><img src={url(picture.poster)} alt={picture.alt} width={picture.width} height={picture.height} loading="lazy"/></button><div><span class="eyebrow">A DIFFERENT KIND OF SCREEN TIME</span><h3>Yes, your terminal<br/>can do that.</h3><p>Play local audio and video. Open pictures. Switch between terminal presentation and an available native window. Your collection gets a front-row seat.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('/docs/playback/')}>Meet the local player →</a></div></div>}</div></section>
  {featured.length > 0 && <section class="section wrap"><div class="section-heading reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / REAL CAPTURES</span><h2>Don’t just read about it.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={url('/showcase/')}>Open the showcase ↗</a></div><div class="media-grid">{featured.map((item, index) => <MediaCard item={item} index={index}/>)}</div></section>}
  <section class="section wrap reveal"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">YOUR LOCAL LIBRARY</span><h2>Keep the moments<br/>worth finding.</h2></div><p>Successful downloads enter a searchable local catalog. Choose other folders to scan, arrange ordered collections, save bookmarks, and resume audio or video.</p></div><Command command={'pinak library scan "path/to/media"'}/><a class="text-link" href={url('/docs/library/')}>Explore Pinak Library →</a></section>
  <section class="ownership section wrap reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / OWN YOUR WORKFLOW</span><h2>Your machine.<br/><span>Your media.</span></h2></div><div class="ownership-copy"><p>Pinak runs where you do. Media is fetched directly by your device and saved to a folder you choose.</p><ul><li>No Pinak account to create.</li><li>No Pinak cloud download service.</li><li>Configuration and history stored locally.</li></ul><p class="small muted">Downloads still connect to their source platforms. Availability depends on those sources, yt-dlp, and installed tools.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('/about/')}>How Pinak works →</a></div></section>
  <section class="section wrap mcp-teaser"><span class="eyebrow">PINAK + YOUR AI APPLICATION</span><h2>Your queue.<br/>A new way to ask.</h2><p>Connect a compatible AI application through MCP. Run it on your device, or host your own remote instance. Queue downloads, inspect progress, and keep control of your files.</p><a class="button button-ghost" href={url('/mcp/')}>Explore Local &amp; Cloud MCP →</a></section>
  <section class="install-banner wrap"><div><span class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT COMMAND</span><h2>Make room for Pinak.</h2><p>Open source. Local first. Ready for your terminal.</p></div><a class="button" href={url('/install/')}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  <MediaViewer items={items}/>
</Layout>
